{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object positioning object positioning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md","fileName":"Object Positioning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Positioning","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Degrees of Freedom","Feedback","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object positioning object positioning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md","fileName":"Object Positioning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Positioning","heading":"Object Positioning","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Object positioning changes the three-dimensional location of an object. It is one of the canonical tasks of [[3D Manipulation]].\n\nThe task can vary by the distance and direction to the initial and target positions, the total translation distance, and the precision required. A direct spatial mapping may make coarse movement intuitive, but large control-display gain can amplify hand jitter and make precise placement difficult.\n\nConstraints can remove unnecessary [[Degrees of Freedom]], while suitable [[Feedback]] helps the user judge when the object has reached the intended location.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Degrees of Freedom","Feedback","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Positioning.md::2","sourceK